WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:04.610
- Hi, I'm Meaghan, and in this video,

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.883
we'll walk through setting
up a class on Khan Academy.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.230
First, log in to Khan Academy.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.690
Once you're logged in,

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.250
you should land on the teacher dashboard.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.470
The teacher dashboard
is the starting point

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.810
for most teacher-focused
activities on Khan Academy

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.723
including creating and organizing classes.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.540
From the teacher dashboard,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.130
make sure you are on the classes tab

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.800
and then click the add new class button

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.710
in the top right corner of the screen.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.230
We recommend that you
create separate classes

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.020
for each group of students you teach.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.280
For example, if you teach four sections

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.600
of seventh grade math,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.883
we recommend you create a
separate class for each section.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.610
If you already use Google Classroom,

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.950
you can import your
classes with all students

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.850
directly to Khan Academy.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.720
If this is not the case, start
by giving your class a name.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.980
A tip we hear from teachers
is to choose a naming system

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.580
that helps keep your
teacher dashboard organized

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.310
and easy to find for both
you and your students.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.070
A common trend is to use your name,

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.943
class period and subject.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.150
Now let's choose one or
more courses for your class.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.140
You can scroll down

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.883
to see the full list of courses available.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.680
You can choose the course by subject

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.830
such as Algebra I or US History

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.270
or you can choose the
course by grade level

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:35.513
like second grade reading or
get ready for fifth grade math.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.570
And don't worry, if you change your mind,

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.480
you can edit your class
name and courses at any time

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.823
in the class settings.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:48.100
After you've set up a class,
you'll want to add students

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.820
and there's three different
ways you can do this.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.850
The first option is to
use Google Classroom.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.270
If you're a teacher who
uses Google Classroom,

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.540
you can link your Google Classroom
and Khan Academy accounts

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.540
to import your class roster directly.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:05.450
This will automatically
send emails to your students

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.033
letting them know they've
been added to your class.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.620
The second option is for
students to join your class

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.490
using the class code.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:18.050
Each class created on Khan
Academy has a unique code

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.593
which students can use to join your class.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.380
Students only need to
enter this code one time

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.910
to be connected to your class.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.120
You can share the code
with students via email

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.770
or by displaying the
code in your classroom.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.140
Students can enter the
code from the teachers tab

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.070
on their learner home.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.840
They will be automatically
added to your class roster

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.373
after they enter the code.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.200
Some teachers find the
process of adding students

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.000
by class code challenging

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.200
especially those with younger students.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.363
But don't worry, we have one more option.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.740
The third option for adding students

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:57.240
is to create accounts for them.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.070
Please remember before
creating accounts for students

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.630
in the United States,

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.360
Khan Academy assumes that
you already have permission

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:08.400
from parents or guardians of
students under the age of 13.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.970
We do not recommend this option

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.240
for students over the age of 13

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.023
as it creates a more
restrictive type of account.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.230
Select the option create
your student account.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.650
When you create these accounts,

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:22.590
Khan Academy automatically generates

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.410
usernames and passwords.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.800
You are able to create the
passwords for your students

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.390
according to preference
and we strongly recommend

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.210
you download the complete
list with login information

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:33.250
to keep in your files

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.000
in case you need to
consult them in the future.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.650
One important warning.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.970
You will only be able
to download this list

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.950
when you create accounts.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.320
You will receive an email with
all this information as well,

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.980
but you will not be able to retrieve

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.550
or edit this information

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:51.083
including passwords at any other time.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.580
Now you've set up a
class and added students.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.610
But what happens when
the class roster changes?

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:01.703
We know students move in and
out of classes during the year.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.040
To keep your student list up to date,

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.600
select the class from
the teacher dashboard

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.600
and in the left side navigation,
select the students tab.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.820
From there, you will be able
to add or remove students

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.670
from your classes.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.850
If a new student is joining your class,

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.770
click add new students and
choose your preferred method

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.960
to add the student from the three methods

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.653
shared earlier in this video.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.980
If one of your students moves
from one class to another

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.820
but remains your student,

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.300
select that student's name
from their current class

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.200
and click on the add to class option.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.060
From here, select the class
the student is joining

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.130
to add them to a new class.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.610
Once that is complete,

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.810
remove the student from the original class

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:48.420
using the remove from class option.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.650
In this situation, you
can move the student

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:52.440
from one class to the other

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.743
without the student needing
to take any additional action.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.090
If you are no longer a student's teacher,

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:02.630
select the student's name
and click stop teaching.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.680
This will remove the student
from all of your class lists

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.330
and disconnect the student's account

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.030
from your teacher account.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.570
You will no longer have access

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.743
to any of this student's information.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.680
If you want to clear
an entire class roster

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.260
like you might wanna do at
the end of a school year,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.340
select the box in the first row

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.710
and then click stop teaching.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.650
This will remove all the
students in that class.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.160
Many teachers recommend
doing this over the summer

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.030
in an effort to clean up your
Khan Academy teacher account

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:35.373
and prevent the accumulation
of students year over year.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.730
One other rostering tip we'd
like to share with you all.

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:44.440
Khan Academy student rosters
are automatically alphabetized,

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.650
but student display names
often appear as their usernames

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:49.700
rather than their real names.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.220
As a teacher, you can edit the
display name of any student

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.100
by hovering over the
name you want to change

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.490
and clicking on the
option edit display name.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.130
Type a new name, save or
hit Enter and you're done.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:06.450
This change will only
occur on your class roster.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.390
It does not appear on
the student's homepage

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.180
nor will it change the data they use

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.943
to log on to Khan Academy.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:16.940
Now that you've completed
the initial setup

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.180
for your classes,

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:20.030
we know you'll probably
want to adjust them

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:22.090
in some way during the school year.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.830
For any changes to the class,

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.970
you want to go to the settings tab.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.240
Here you can edit the class name,

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.480
change the course or courses,

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.550
update student sync with Google Classroom,

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:36.680
sign up for a weekly report
on student performance,

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.260
and even delete the class.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.210
We hope this video helps you get started

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.593
building your own classes on Khan Academy.

